  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 311 AM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nSunday: Heat continues to build on Sunday, with highs in the low\nto mid 90s and heat index values around 100. Could again see\nshowers and storms Saturday night into Sunday (15-25% chance). \n\nMonday and Tuesday: These will be the hottest days in the\nforecast period as a plume of even hotter air (850mb temps\npossibly exceeding 24C) moves overhead ahead of a cold front.\nLook for highs in the mid 90s to around 100 with heat index\nvalues of 100-105. HeatRisk shows values of moderate to major.\n\nWednesday and Thursday:\n\nA cold front moves through later in the day Tuesday, bringing\nhighs in the mid 80s to low 90s. NW flow looks to become\nestablished, so thunderstorm complexes may become an issue. At\nthis time, there is enough uncertainty on that aspect of the\nforecast to not get into specifics.",
